# What's new — shown once per installed version in the app.
# One `## <version>` section per release; the lines below it are the notes.
# Keep the matching full entry in the repository's CHANGELOG.md.

## 7.20.0
- Login is now opt-in. A fresh install has no account and opens with no sign-in, so a local, single-user setup gets no password prompt. To protect a shared or LAN instance, add an account with `--create-user NAME`; then sign-in is required until you delete `users.json`. The public `admin` / `admin` default account is gone.

## 7.18.0
- The app now ships a built-in help with a 3-level tutorial (Beginner, Intermediate, Expert) and task-focused "How to?" recipes. Open it with F1 or the ? button in the top panel.

## 7.17.0
- Updates now wait out a briefly-locked file instead of failing (mainly Windows), and the launcher/installer scripts are POSIX sh so they also work on systems without bash. The app has so far been used on Debian-based Linux; macOS, other Linux distributions and Windows run the same Python core and are new territory — feedback is welcome, and `ybe uninstall` undoes it cleanly.

## 7.16.0
- Windows is now supported: install natively with the PowerShell bootstrap (ybx.ps1) or the Python installer, and run every ybe command (start/stop/status/logs/update/uninstall) the same as on Linux and macOS. The installer adds ybe to your PATH and starts/stops the server with Windows APIs.

## 7.15.0
- The ybe command and the installer now run on Python instead of shell scripts, so every ybe command (start/stop/status/logs/update/uninstall) behaves the same on Linux and macOS. Install and update downloads use Python instead of curl, so only Python 3 is required.

## 7.14.0
- Fixed: `ybe status` no longer reports the app as running when it is not. A leftover ybe.pid could point at an unrelated process that later reused the same PID; the launcher now confirms the process is really the app, so status, stop, upgrade and uninstall are accurate.

## 7.13.0
- Dragging or drawing a box no longer redraws every other box: the image and untouched boxes are cached and only the active box is repainted, so the pointer stays fluid on images with hundreds of boxes.

## 7.12.0
- Dragging a box no longer updates the side panel on every mouse move; the box row syncs once when you release the mouse. Dragging stays responsive on images with many boxes.

## 7.11.0
- New action and shortcut for a minimal box view: press `,` to hide the resize anchors, the class label and the `x` / `/` corner buttons so only the box outlines remain. Press it again to show them; the choice is remembered across reloads.

## 7.10.0
- A reload button (↻) now sits beside the Split selector. It re-scans the image folders and re-runs the active filter chain for the selected split, keeping you on the same image.
- Changing the split now shows a spinner at the Split control and briefly blocks the selector and reload button while the list (and filter chain) updates.

## 7.9.0
- Two new built-in filters: Has tag and Does not have tag. Pick the tag from a dropdown filled from your tags.yaml (options: {DATASET_TAG_NAMES}); filters honour a custom tags folder via {TAGS_DIR}.
- Fixed: the tag_image.py helper no longer mangles paths that merely contain "images" (e.g. images_backup) and can write to a custom tags folder; actions get a {TAGS_DIR} placeholder.

## 7.8.0
- Running an action or hook no longer pops up a result window or a success toast. A successful run is logged to the browser console; a failure shows a toast with the reason.

## 7.7.0
- Fixed: creating or resizing a box no longer gets slow on images with many boxes. Only the box you are dragging is updated while you drag, so the pointer stays responsive.

## 7.6.0
- Fixed: the app no longer becomes heavy, laggy or sluggish after you browse many images. Each image is decoded once and its memory is released as soon as you move on, so long sessions stay responsive.

## 7.5.0
- Four new built-in actions you can run from an action or hook step: app_select_next_box, app_select_prev_box, app_clear_tags and app_copy_labels_from_prev (copy the previous image's boxes and tags).

## 7.4.0
- Change password and Sign out moved from the side panel's top bar into a new Settings > Account tab (it appears only when sign-in is enabled).

## 7.3.0
- The developer debug console and auto-reloader are now off by default, so an error page can no longer run code for anyone who reaches the app. If you are developing, pass `--flask-debug`. The `--debug` flag is unchanged: it only adds verbose logging to the browser console.

## 7.2.0
- Starting the app as the root user is now refused: it would make your files root-owned and run the debug server with root privileges. If you really need it (for example inside a container), pass `--allow-root`.

## 7.1.0
- Signing in now survives a restart. The session key is saved in `.secret_key` in your user folder (owner-only), so `ybe restart` and `ybe update` no longer sign you out. The file is kept across updates; delete it if you want to force everyone to sign in again.

## 7.0.0
- The app now asks you to sign in. It ships with a ready-to-use account so `ybe start` works with no extra setup: username `admin`, password `admin`. Change the password from the side panel (the key button: Change password) after the first sign in.
- Accounts live in `users.json` in your user folder, stored hashed (never as plain text) and owner-only. Admins can also manage them from the command line: `--create-user NAME` prompts for the password with no echo, and `--list-users` shows the names. The side panel also has Sign out.
- This is a convenience gate for a trusted network, not strong security: over plain http the password is sent in clear text, and the default password is public until you change it.

## 6.9.0
- Creating an action, hook or filter now looks like an editor: a titled header, grouped sections (Details, Steps, After success, Arguments) and a sticky Create / Clear footer. Command and argument fields are shown in monospace.

## 6.8.0
- Settings > Actions and Hooks now have Create / Existing sub-tabs, matching the Filters tab.
- The Settings window now sizes to the content of the active tab (capped at 620px) instead of filling the screen.

## 6.7.0
- The filter chain now has a "+ Add filter" button and an "x" on each row to remove one (up to 8 filters can be chained).
- Applying a filter chain shows a spinner on Apply and closes Settings when it finishes.

## 6.6.0
- Settings > Filters is now split into three sub-tabs — Active chain, Create and Library — instead of one long page. The Active chain sub-tab notes that up to 8 filters chain top to bottom.

## 6.5.0
- The last image you were on is now remembered across browsers: open the app in another browser and it resumes where you left off (per dataset and split).
- Your app state now lives in one file, config.json, in the user folder. The old .recent_data_yamls.json, .view_state.json and .settings.json are merged into it automatically on first start and then removed.

## 6.4.0
- Disable a hook or action for the current dataset only, without deleting its file: use the "Enabled for this dataset" checkbox in Settings > Actions / Hooks. A disabled action's button disappears and a disabled hook does not fire; re-check it to turn it back on. The setting is remembered per dataset and never changes the extension file.

## 6.1.0
- Fixed: the app no longer becomes laggy after you view many images. Each image load now releases the previous decoded image first, so memory does not keep growing the longer you browse.

## 6.0.0
- Create actions, hooks and filters from the web UI (Settings > Actions / Hooks / Filters): fill in the form and the app writes valid YAML for you, so indentation, `:` and `-` mistakes are impossible.
- Click a placeholder button to insert tokens like {IMAGE_PATH} or {INPUT_PIPE} into a command, so you do not have to memorise their spelling.
- Extension YAML files now carry an `api_version`. Files with a missing/older version can be opened in a raw YAML editor and saved (comments are preserved and the version is bumped); files newer than the app are blocked with a warning.
- Files without `api_version` still load; the editor is how you bring them up to date. The shipped filters declare `api_version: 1`.
- Fixed: Undo/Redo now work for drawing a box, moving, resizing and changing a box's class from the canvas picker. These edits previously left the undo history empty, so Undo and the Z shortcut did nothing.

## 5.0.0
- Filters are now defined by YAML in filters/: name, description, active, arguments (name/required/default/options) and steps. Put the filter's script under scripts/ and call it from a step.
- Steps get the action placeholders plus {DATA_YAML_PATH}, {DATASET_PATH}, {SPLIT}, {INPUT_PIPE}, {OUTPUT_PIPE}; each argument is usable in place as {NAME}. Use {PYTHON} (the app's interpreter) instead of `python`.
- Settings > Filters shows the name, a trimmed description and an input per argument; active:false filters are hidden.
- New shipped Contains class / Does not contain class filters; options: {DATASET_CLASS_NAMES} fills the dropdown from the dataset classes and invalid values are rejected.
- app/filters/example.yaml is a working example backed by app/scripts/example_filter.py; the old filters/*.py form is removed.

## 4.0.0
- The control panel now sits on the left by default; change it in Settings > Layout > Control panel side.
- Saving an image now writes its labels and tags together: the image's tag file is written and new tag names are added to tags.yaml. Tag edits are saved with the image instead of instantly.
- Tag edits now work with Undo/Redo (Z / Y).
- Removed the built-in update_tags action and the shipped on_after_save hook; on_after_save is still a valid event for your own hooks.
- API: /api/labels is now /api/annotations (returns boxes and tags); /api/tags and /api/tags.yaml were removed.

## 3.6.0
- Fixed: tags.yaml is now read as a plain list (`- tag` per line, as written by dataset_autotag.py), so the tag bar shows every tag. A nested `tags:` key is ignored and saving rewrites the file as a plain list.

## 3.5.0
- Settings > Shortcuts now has an Edit view: click a binding and press the new key combination, then Save. Changes are written to your own shortcuts.txt (the shipped one is left alone), and a reset button restores the default.

## 3.4.2
- Fixed: on a fresh install the Load a dataset, What's new and Tip of the day dialogs no longer appear at the same time; they now show one after another.

## 3.4.1
- Fixed: the installer now reliably creates the ybe alias even when a stale ybe symlink or directory is already in the launcher folder.

## 3.4.0
- A daily tip dialog now suggests one random feature each day.
- New built-in update_tags action (run after save by a shipped on_after_save hook) adds new tag names to tags.yaml on demand.
- Per-dataset Tags folder setting; the tag bar warns when a tag is missing from tags.yaml.
- Settings > View is now Settings > General, with a Show tip on start toggle; the README is a lighter quick start with docs/ for details.
- Fixed: choosing All splits no longer snaps back to the previously selected split. The last image is now remembered per split.

## 3.3.0
- UI settings (View/Layout, panel sizes, floating-window positions) are saved on the server too, so a new browser starts with your setup. A value you change in a browser still wins there.

## 3.2.0
- Settings > Layout now has a block per widget with a Show toggle and a Location selector.
- Tags are visible by default; the old View > Tags switch is gone.

## 3.1.0
- Actions, Navigation (Prev / counter / Next) and Save / Undo are now dockable widgets like Tags and Boxes.
- The bottom panel hides when it holds no widget; the box list no longer adds inner padding.

## 3.0.0
- Updates are done with `ybe update` (alias `ybe upgrade`); `ybx.sh` is only the installer. The launchers are always added to ~/.local/bin (the `--no-link` option is gone).

## 2.16.0
- Tags and Boxes are now dockable widgets: send them to the left, right or bottom panel, or keep them floating. A panel only appears while it holds a widget.

## 2.13.0
- Releases for major/minor version bumps are now tagged and published automatically on GitHub.

## 2.12.0
- Added `ybx.sh uninstall` / `ybe uninstall`: removes the app, venv and launchers but keeps your files; `--purge --yes` removes the whole folder.

## 2.11.0
- Added `ybx.sh update --latest` (newest commit on main) and `ybx.sh update --commit <sha>`; both work over HTTP without git.

## 2.10.0
- `ybx.sh install` / `upgrade` now start the app automatically (background) and restart a running instance; use `--no-start` to skip.

## 2.9.0
- New Layout settings: choose the panel side (left/right) and detach Tags or Boxes into movable floating windows.
- Float windows snap to a screen edge on release (or use the L/T/R/B buttons); their position is remembered.

## 2.8.0
- Added a first-run "Load a dataset" dialog: paste a data.yaml path and click Load.
- Settings now uses tabs (View / Dataset / Shortcuts / Updates); the dataset dropdown, path input and Load button sit on one row.
- Replaced the breaking-change warnings with a "What's new" changelog, shown once after the app updates to a new version.
- `ybe check-update` no longer prints the `breaking_changes:` and `breaking_notes:` lines.
